{"parentUuid":"70027f36-014c-471c-b679-83442b5f115a","isSidechain":false,"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Base directory for this skill: /Users/pfleidi/.claude/skills/verify\n\n# Full Project Verification\n\n## 1. Discover Verification Commands\n\nInspect the project to determine how to build, lint, and test. Check these sources in order — stop as soon as you find definitive commands for each category (build, lint, test):\n\n1. **Makefile** — look for `build`, `lint`, `check`, `test`, `ci`, `verify` targets\n2. **mise** — check for `.mise.toml` or `.mise/*.toml`. Look for `[tasks]` definitions. If found, use `mise run <task>`.\n3. **CI workflows** — read `.github/workflows/*.yml` (or `.gitlab-ci.yml`, etc.) to find the exact commands CI runs\n4. **README.md** — look for \"Development\", \"Contributing\", \"Building\", or \"Testing\" sections\n5. **Package manager conventions** — detect from project files:\n   - `go.mod` → `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`, `staticcheck ./...`, `go test ./...`\n   - `package.json` → check `scripts` for `build`, `lint`, `test`\n   - `Cargo.toml` → `cargo build`, `cargo clippy`, `cargo test`\n   - `pyproject.toml` / `setup.py` → check for configured linters, `pytest`\n\nBriefly state which source you used and what commands you will run.\n\n## 2. Run Verification\n\nRun the discovered commands sequentially. Show the COMPLETE, unedited output of every command. Never summarize, truncate, or paraphrase.\n\nThe commands should cover, at minimum:\n- **Build** — the project compiles without errors\n- **Lint / static analysis** — no lint warnings or static analysis failures\n- **Tests** — the test suite passes\n\nUse the exact commands, flags, and build tags found in step 1. Do not invent your own flags.\n\n## 3. Report\n\nAfter all commands have run:\n\n- If ALL exited 0: report \"All green\" and paste the test summary line.\n- If ANY failed: report exactly which commands failed. Paste the failing output in full.\n\nDo NOT fix anything automatically. Do NOT suggest fixes. Just report the results and STOP.\n"}]},"isMeta":true,"uuid":"7320748d-d359-4549-bff5-b03d98c25abf","timestamp":"2026-04-23T00:17:58.909Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/pfleidi/entire/cli/.worktrees/feat/checkpoints-v2-close-test-gaps","sessionId":"e72f3c16-a73d-4eb6-a92d-4bfeb62a91b9","version":"2.1.104","gitBranch":"feat/checkpoints-v2-close-test-gaps"}
