r reused in broader contexts, adding `filepath.Base(sessionID)` sanitization at line 547 would be prudent. Same applies to the `createFile` function (line 466-475) which joins `dir` with a regex-extracted `path` from prompts -- but again, only test-controlled inputs reach it.\n\n---\n\n### Area 2: GitHub Actions workflow injection (e2e-checkpoints-v2.yml:49-51)\n\n**Status: Not a risk**\n\nThe workflow uses `${{ inputs.agent }}` and `${{ inputs.checkpoints_mode }}` in `env:` context (lines 49-51), not in a `run:` context. Both inputs are further constrained to `type: choice` with enumerated options (lines 8-28). The `run:` command is the static string `mise run test:e2e:canary`. There is no script injection vector here.\n\nThe `somecredstorepass` string at line 43 is a dummy keyring unlock password used identically in `ci.yml`, `e2e.yml`, and other existing workflows. It is not a real credential -- it is required to initialize GNOME Keyring in headless CI.\n\n---\n\n### Area 3: `ensureHookEntireBinary` symlink/copy (e2e/tests/main_test.go:84-102)\n\n**Status: Not a risk**\n\nThis function creates a symlink (or file copy on Windows) from the test binary to `entire` in the same directory. The source path `entireBin` comes from `E2E_ENTIRE_BIN`, which is set by the build system. The target `hookBin` is always `filepath.Join(dir, \"entire\")` where `dir` is `filepath.Dir(entireBin)`. The `filepath.Clean` equality check at line 87 prevents creating a self-referential link. This runs only during test setup (`TestMain`), not in production code.\n\n---\n\n### Area 4: `runOutputEnv` environment injection (e2e/entire/entire.go:180-195)\n\n**Status: Not a risk**\n\nThe `AttachWithEnv` and `runOutputEnv` functions accept `extraEnv []string` and append them to `cmd.Env`. All callers are test code with hardcoded values like `[]string{\"HOME=\" + homeDir}`. There is no path from user input to these env vars.\n\n---\n\n### Area 5: `vogonHomeDir` temp directory predictability (e2e/agents/vogon.go:145-152)\n\n**Status: Not a risk**\n\nThe function creates `os.TempDir()/vogon-e2e-home-&lt;sha256[:12]&gt;` with 0755 permissions. The SHA256 is derived from the repo directory path. While the name is deterministic given the same input, this runs only in test infrastructure. The directory permissions are appropriate for a HOME directory substitute in test contexts.\n\n---\n\n### Area 6: `checkpointsMode()` unvalidated env var passthrough (e2e/testutil/repo.go:190-199)\n\n**Status: Low-impact logic issue, not a security risk**\n\nThe `checkpointsMode()` function has a `default: return mode` arm that passes through any unrecognized `E2E_CHECKPOINTS_MODE` value. This causes `primaryCheckpointRef()` to return the v1 ref for unknown modes (hitting the `default` case at line 205). Meanwhile, `ApplySuiteCheckpointsMode()` at line 181 will `t.Fatalf` on unknown modes. The inconsistency means an invalid mode would fail fast in `ApplySuiteCheckpointsMode` but silently degrade in `primaryCheckpointRef`. This is a correctness observation, not a security finding.\n\n---\n\n### Area 7: Race conditions in checkpoint polling\n\n**Status: Acceptable by design**\n\nThe `WaitForCheckpoint`, `WaitForCheckpointAdvanceFrom`, and `WaitForSessionIdle` functions use polling loops with `time.Sleep(200ms)` intervals. These are inherently TOCTOU patterns -- the state could change between the check and subsequent assertions. However, this is the standard approach for E2E test infrastructure where you are waiting for async processes (git hooks) to complete. The timeouts and polling intervals are appropriate for the test context.\n\n---\n\n### Area 8: No secrets or credentials in code\n\nVerified: No API keys, tokens, passwords, or sensitive credentials are introduced in this diff. The `somecredstorepass` is an existing pattern for CI keyring initialization, not a real secret.\n\n---\n\n### Summary\n\n**Verdict: No security issues found.**\n\nAll changed code is test infrastructur