turns `mode`. The second case is unreachable because it does the same thing as the default. The explicit case listing of known modes gives a false impression that unknown modes are handled differently.\n\n**Suggested fix:** Simplify to:\n\n```go\nfunc checkpointsMode() string {\n    mode := os.Getenv(\"E2E_CHECKPOINTS_MODE\")\n    if mode == \"\" || mode == checkpointsModeLegacy {\n        return checkpointsModeLegacy\n    }\n    return mode\n}\n```\n\n### 6. Unnecessary private wrapper: `applySuiteCheckpointsMode`\n\n**e2e/testutil/repo.go:185-188** -- The private `applySuiteCheckpointsMode` is called exactly once (line 112) and is a trivial delegation to the exported `ApplySuiteCheckpointsMode`. This adds an indirection that serves no purpose.\n\n**Suggested fix:** Call `ApplySuiteCheckpointsMode(t, dir)` directly on line 112 and remove the private wrapper.\n\n### 7. Unnecessary comment in attach test\n\n**cmd/entire/cli/attach_test.go:108** (in `TestAttach_CheckpointsVersion2`) -- The test body is self-explanatory from its function name and the existing doc comment on `setAttachCheckpointsVersion2Enabled`. No inline comments needed beyond what's already there.\n\nThis is borderline cosmetic, so feel free to ignore.\n\n## Praise\n\n- The `mergeSettings` / `cloneSettingsMap` recursive merge in `e2e/testutil/repo.go` is a clean replacement for the previous shallow key-copy in `PatchSettings`. It correctly preserves existing `strategy_options` when adding new ones, which was the root cause of test fragility.\n\n- The `ensureHookEntireBinary` function in `e2e/tests/main_test.go` is well-designed: it handles the Windows copy fallback, uses symlinks on Unix, and correctly short-circuits when the binary is already named `entire`.\n\n- The `vogon --write-session` mode is a good design choice for attach tests -- it gives deterministic transcript setup without firing hooks, keeping the attach test focused on `entire attach` behavior rather than full agent lifecycle.\n\n- The `PushCheckpointRefs` and `CheckpointMetadataRef` helpers in `e2e/testutil/repo.go` properly abstract the v1/v2 ref differences, making the existing `resume_remote_test.go` work correctly across all three checkpoint modes without per-mode test branching.\n\n- The `CommitIfDirty` helper is a pragmatic addition -- it handles the case where `entire enable` in a clone is already idempotent, preventing \"nothing to commit\" failures.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Overall assessment: APPROVE with minor fixes**\n\nThe branch adds solid test coverage for checkpoints v2 across E2E, integration, and unit test layers. The architecture choices (mode-aware ref helpers, vogon write-session mode, recursive settings merge) are sound.\n\nThe main areas to clean up are:\n- The dead `entire.Attach()` function (finding 1)\n- The duplicated `shadowBranches` function (finding 2)\n- Two copy-paste-with-variation patterns (findings 3 and 4) that should be unified\n\nEstimated effort to address: 30-45 minutes for findings 1-4. Findings 5-6 are optional and take 5 minutes total.</result>\n<usage><total_tokens>96637</total_tokens><tool_uses>40</tool_uses><duration_ms>178603</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
